<AboutPage
  region="usa"
  title="For corporate sponsors | doorbell.life"
  h1="How can a company sponsor doorbell.life?"
  description="Companies can put their own brand look on the public-service notices shown on error pages and get view reports. Sponsorship plans are still being designed; email us to talk."
  lead="Sponsorship plans are still being designed. If your company is interested, email contact@doorbell.life."
>
  <h2>What would a sponsor get?</h2>
  <p>Here’s what we’re planning. The final terms will be worked out with each sponsor:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Brand look: the public-service cards on error pages can use the company’s colors, fonts, logo, or mascot.</li>
    <li>View reports: how many times the notices were shown and clicked.</li>
    <li>ESG impact report: a downloadable report for the company’s sustainability reporting.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Can the brand appear on every topic?</h2>
  <p>No. Topics like animals and blood donation can use the full brand look. Missing-person notices always use a neutral style, with the brand shown only in small text in a corner. If brand materials are reported as inappropriate, we pause them first.</p>

  <h2>Where do the report numbers come from?</h2>
  <p>From sampling: we record 1 in every 10 displays and multiply back up in the report. We count only the website’s domain, the topic, the country, and the date. No cookies, and no visitor IP addresses.</p>

  <h2>How do I get in touch?</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@doorbell.life">contact@doorbell.life</a> with your company name and the topics you’d like to sponsor.</p>
</AboutPage>
